    <entry>
        <title>Sugar-Free Fries &amp; Other Lies</title>
        <author>
            <name>Azal</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://zuzulableue.com/sugar-free-fries-and-other-lies/"/>
        <id>https://zuzulableue.com/sugar-free-fries-and-other-lies/</id>
        <media:content url="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/zero-sugar_fries_cover.png" medium="image" />
            <category term="Essays"/>

        <updated>2026-08-14T02:33:25+03:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/zero-sugar_fries_cover.png" alt="lonely but in my alo set + matcha " />
                    STOP PROMOTING UR SUGAR-FREE FRIES AND KETO YOGURTS. The wellness craze in&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/zero-sugar_fries_cover.png" class="type:primaryImage" alt="lonely but in my alo set + matcha " /></p>
                <p class="align-center">STOP PROMOTING UR SUGAR-FREE FRIES AND KETO YOGURTS.</p>
<p>The wellness craze in Lebanon is out of control. Around summer 2024 with an absolute PEAK in spring 2025, collagen smoothie places and random pilates studios hatched at every street corner of Beirut.</p>
<p>I am not talking about Backburner; that place was always around, even if it turned into an overpriced "to-be-seen" hub overnight. I mean places like The Glow Paradise. There are dozens like it now, but it's their toxic marketing feeding young girls lies about wellness that specifically pisses me. </p>
<p>I won't even questioning their ingredient quality. At those prices, I pray to GOD it's top tier (though I’d love to know the actual farm names for this supposed local "grass-fed beef" in Lebanon, because IT IS THOSE farmers who deserve real recognition after the crisis). No, what gets me is the 3-digit label right next to every marvelously named food item on their menu: the calorie count.</p>
<p>How MANY TIMES have I stumbled on videos of influencers my age trying the Glow matcha that "only has 120 kcal guys"!!!!! It exasperates me.</p>
<p>One, because these influencers usually have absolutely no clue what the hell they are talking about. They scan their meals every day with an AI calorie counter app, then complain to their followers about having a crumb of sponge cake.</p>
<p>I am not attacking those influencers. But as someone who has suffered with an eating disorder, I can't sit and watch people PROMOTING that kind of stuff to others. If someone is struggling, I hope from the bottom of my heart that they have the support they need, but please save that for tumblr thinspo and not the FYP of a random tween who has never even heard of calories before.</p>
<p>Also, it is incredibly interesting that "healthful" foods are systematically marketed to women. Look at The Glow Paradise's posts: women in bikinis or tight little Alo Yoga sets posing with a "protein papa" juice. It’s alarming how seamlessly Western activewear branding is pushing Eurocentric body standards onto Arab women. Or simply look at the captions: "youthful face," "rejuvenation," "game changer for skin health"... They are selling anti-aging to a clientele made of teens and young adults.</p>
<p>Helloo???? What about ESSENTIAL health?</p>
<figure class="post__image align-center"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/IMG_4847.jpeg" alt="no clue who these ladies are, but like u get the alo pilates matcha vibe " width="379" height="379" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" srcset="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/responsive/IMG_4847-xs.jpeg 300w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/responsive/IMG_4847-sm.jpeg 480w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/responsive/IMG_4847-md.jpeg 768w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/21/responsive/IMG_4847-lg.jpeg 1024w"></figure>
<p>It blows my mind how our society continuously mistakes a woman’s physical appearance for actual "health" instead of her internal organ function.</p>
<p>Obviously one follows the other: if your body is operating <em>right</em> internally, the rest shows. But when young girls end up chronically undereating because they are terrified of calories, believe me it will completely <em>wreck </em>their fertility, bone density, and actual hair health. No amount of collagen powder saves your endocrine system when you are running a massive calorie deficit lol.</p>
<p>Posting those HYPER-curated bodies sets impossibly toxic expectations, especially for Arab girls. I am not generalizing, but from <em>actual</em> experience, observation, and like basic scientific facts, Arab female physiognomy (fat distribution, bone structures…)is BIOLOGICLLY, different from that of ultra-lean Western French sticks!</p>
<p>To make matters worse, they are hypocritically <span class="rQesXe MPyX">flooding</span> their Insta feed with words like "nourish, nourish, nourish." Like they even have weight loss plans. I have no clue <em>how</em> they interact with their clients, but I really hope they inform them properly instead of throwing them into a giant orthorexia pit.</p>
<p>(Uhm, so side note: I realized I keep saying "they." When I say "they," I mean The Glow Paradise. But let's be real this <em>predatory</em> pattern exists everywhere in the world,not just Beirut)</p>
<p>ALSO, I am not saying people should be completely oblivious to the energetic values of what they ingest! I would be a crazy person and healthcare worker if I discouraged <em>basic</em> nutritional literacy. Take the US or Canada, if there was no nutritional info on menus, people would spend their whole daily energy expenditure on one peameal bacon bagel. So we need to educate people in a realistic and scientific way!</p>
<p>Yes, whole foods are best for our bodies. Yes, everything is processed nowadays. But surprise surprise, whole foods today are ALSO processed. So when you spend $11 on four pieces of organic chicken nuggets, each the size of my thumb, or a sad little omelette, you are 1. wasting money and 2. missing the actual experience of going out to eat. You can make all of that at home for a quarter of the price. Stop being so gullible to aesthetic pastel colored pretty plates and the vibe of a place just to avoid looking at what you are actually ingesting. (If you want an example of a spot actually doing healthful food right, look at places like Honest Greens).</p>
<p>The best thing in my and EXPERTS' opinion (it should be standard advice, really) is to eat healthy at home. And by HEALTHY, I mean eat the rainbow, avoid processed dairy products or heavy store-bought dressings, ditch the zero-sugar carbonated drinks (the chemical additives damage ur gut microbiome)… Then, when you TREAT yourself by going out, have something you CANNOT cook at home. We have normalized eating out so much today when it used to be a luxury!</p>
<p>All this to say: before getting sucked into the goop-flavored black hole of wellness aesthetic, please educate yourself, and please please please be careful with what you consume online. If you are ever in need of support, please reach out to your loved ones. I never want anyone to feel like they aren't good enough. Love yourself and be kind to others.</p>
<p><!-- notionvc: 418a1535-fd9b-42f7-8cc6-ee7e835b3a59 --></p>
            ]]>
        </content>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title>La Gazelle de Waller</title>
        <author>
            <name>Azal</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://zuzulableue.com/la-gazelle-de-waller/"/>
        <id>https://zuzulableue.com/la-gazelle-de-waller/</id>
        <media:content url="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/zuzugazelle.jpg" medium="image" />
            <category term="Culture"/>

        <updated>2026-07-23T23:06:15+03:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/zuzugazelle.jpg" alt="" />
                    Imaginez la personne la plus chic, la plus discrète et la plus&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/zuzugazelle.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <p data-path-to-node="3">Imaginez la personne la plus chic, la plus discrète et la plus cultivée que vous puissiez croiser : c'est exactement ce que j'appelle une Gazelle de Waller. J'ai tenu à ce que ma toute première publication ici soit consacrée à ce concept parce qu'il me semble indispensable que mes lecteurs et lectrices observent le monde à travers cette grille de lecture, ne serait-ce que pour saisir le fil conducteur de mes prochains posts.</p>
<figure class="post__image align-center"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/IMG_4815.jpeg" alt="Gazelle de Waller" width="254" height="230" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" srcset="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/IMG_4815-xs.jpeg 300w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/IMG_4815-sm.jpeg 480w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/IMG_4815-md.jpeg 768w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/IMG_4815-lg.jpeg 1024w"></figure>
<p data-path-to-node="4">Bon, retour à notre sujet. Une Gazelle de Waller, c’est quelqu’un qui n’a absolument rien à prouver (<i data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="197">when ykyk</i>). C'est le produit d'un confort générationnel familial qui dépasse les simples critères financiers "d'aisance". <span data-subtree="aimfl,mfl" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);">Elle doit venir d'une famille éduquée respectable qui a de bonnes valeurs et toujours attachée à ses traditions.</span><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></p>
<div class="Fsg96" data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>
<p data-path-to-node="5">Chez la Gazelle de Waller, le luxe n'a rien d'ostentatoire. Puisque, justement, elle a grandi dans un environnement raffiné, pour elle, c'est tout à fait normal d'être entourée de ce qu'il y'a de mieux. Alors quand je parle de luxe, je ne fais évidemment PAS référence aux it-bags de la saison, à la logomania ou à tout ce qui crie sa marque à dix mètres (<i data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="328">l'horreur absolue</i>). Je fais plutôt référence à choisir systématiquement ce qu’il y a de plus noble comme matière sans jamais opter pour ce qui est facilement identifiable (qu'il s'agisse d'un cuir de veau Box pleine fleur, d'une pure vigogne, ou d'une soie grège brute). Bref, le savoir-faire et la durabilité priment sur tout le reste.</p>
<figure class="post__image"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.10.55-2.png" alt="Soie grège et selvedge denim" width="2540" height="1010" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" srcset="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.10.55-2-xs.png 300w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.10.55-2-sm.png 480w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.10.55-2-md.png 768w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.10.55-2-lg.png 1024w"></figure>
<p data-path-to-node="6">Cette même exigence se retrouve dans son rapport aux autres. La bienséance et l'étiquette chez la Gazelle de Waller sont instinctivement intégrées. Elle sait où aller, comment se comporter, quoi dire, quand se taire. On peut aussi bien la croiser emmitouflée dans un manteau vintage seconde-main au lobby d'un grand hôtel parisien qu'attablée le lendemain sur un tabouret en plastique au cœur d'une médina, un thé à la menthe à la main. Tout cela bien évidemment sans perdre sa confiance et sa noblesse. </p>
<p data-path-to-node="7">Son érudition ferait <span class="rQesXe MPyX">pâlir les théories de Bourdieu sur le capital culturel</span> : elle comprend l'art, la haute parfumerie, la gastronomie, les matières et la littérature... Même en voyage, la quête d'authenticité prend le dessus sur les adresses <i data-path-to-node="7" data-index-in-node="230">trendy</i> de la saison. Elle préfère une petite table dénichée au coin d'une ruelle plutôt qu'un resto où tout le monde se presse et fait la queue.</p>
<figure class="post__image"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.51.21.png" alt="medina + resto" width="2312" height="836" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" srcset="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.51.21-xs.png 300w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.51.21-sm.png 480w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.51.21-md.png 768w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.51.21-lg.png 1024w"></figure>
<p data-path-to-node="8">Dans son univers discret (qu'il ne faudrait SURTOUT pas le confondre avec de l'hésitation ou de la timidité) chaque détail autour d'elle est minutieusement observé. On pourrait facilement passer à côté d'une Gazelle de Waller sur le trottoir sans y prêter attention, mais pour quiconque sait vraiment observer, sa présence finit toujours par triompher.</p>
<p data-path-to-node="10"><strong data-path-to-node="10" data-index-in-node="0">P.S.</strong> Pourquoi ce nom ? Parce que la Gazelle de Waller  (aussi connu sous le nom de Gérénuk) est sans doute l'animal rare le plus absurdement élégant de la savane, ne vivant qu'en très petit groupe. Considérez désormais ce blog comme leur point de ralliement.</p>
<p data-path-to-node="11"><strong data-path-to-node="11" data-index-in-node="0">P.S. 2 :</strong> La vraie Gazelle de Waller, c'est ma Mima (et ses sœurs). </p>
<figure class="post__image"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.18.41.png" alt="My mima and her sisters" width="2826" height="1358" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" srcset="https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.18.41-xs.png 300w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.18.41-sm.png 480w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.18.41-md.png 768w ,https://zuzulableue.com/media/posts/13/responsive/Screenshot-2026-08-09-at-13.18.41-lg.png 1024w"></figure>
            ]]>
        </content>
